Add a "ram" widget to MacShell's bar: RAM in use in GB (MemTotal - MemAvailable, same figure as `free`'s "used"), with a memory-module icon (new Glyph kind "ram"), a warning colour at >=75% (orange) / >=85% (red), and a click that opens btop in the configured terminal. Polling pauses while Game Mode is on or the bar is hidden.

Apply (a MacShell update may overwrite MacBar.qml, so re-apply afterwards):
  cd ~/.local/share/macshell/MacShell && patch -p1 < <repo>/macshell/ram-widget.patch
Then enable it by adding "ram" to "barWidgets" in ~/.config/macbar/settings.json.
settings.json is only read at load, so trigger a reload (edit any MacShell .qml, or restart MacShell).

